"""
zhou_replication.py
===================
Farm-level hedging effectiveness for French winter wheat.

Framework
---------
Implements a Zhou, Li & Pai (2016)-style farm-level hedging evaluation
framework with Möllmann et al. (2019)-style data-driven period selection,
using the forecast-plus-residual-bootstrap pricing engine from
pricing_comparison.py.

References:
  Zhou, Li & Pai (2016): "Hedging crop yield with exchange-traded weather
    derivatives", Agricultural Finance Review, 76(1), 172–186.
  Möllmann, Buchholz & Musshoff (2019): "Comparing the hedging effectiveness
    of weather derivatives based on remotely sensed vegetation health indices
    and meteorological indices", Weather, Climate, and Society, 11, 33–48.

Period selection (Möllmann et al. 2019, Section 2b)
---------------------------------------------------
For each region × OOS year, the optimal CDD accumulation window is found
on calibration data by maximising |Spearman(cCDD, detrended yield)|:

  1. Detrend yield: ln(Y_t) = a + b·t + ε_t  [OLS on calibration data]
  2. Search all 21 start ≤ end combinations within March–August
  3. Select window with highest |Spearman(cCDD, detrended yield)|
  4. Strike K = mean(actual cCDD in optimal window over calibration years)
  5. Spearman correlation reported; selection and evaluation metrics differ
     (acknowledged as a stated methodological choice following Möllmann)

Pricing (identical engine to pricing_comparison.py)
----------------------------------------------------
  T_sim = model_forecast[optimal_window] + block_bootstrap(OOS_residuals)
  cCDD_sim = sum(max(0, T_sim − T_ref))
  Price = exp(−r·TTM) · E[TICK · max(cCDD_sim − K, 0)]

Hedge ratio (Zhou et al. 2016, fixed common K)
-----------------------------------------------
  N*(sv) via 1-D semi-variance minimisation (K fixed = calibration mean)
  N*(var) via Johnson (1960) analytical formula (K fixed)

Primary metric: HE(SV) — semi-variance reduction (downside protection)
Wilcoxon: H0: median HE(SV) = 0  |  H1: > 0  (one-sided, α = 0.05)

What departs from Zhou et al.
------------------------------
  - Period selection: Möllmann et al. data-driven vs. Zhou's fixed JJA
  - Strike: calibration-period mean (vs. Zhou's jointly optimised K)
  - Pricing: block-bootstrap (vs. Zhou's FHS calibrated to CME)
  - Index: CDD T_ref=10°C (vs. Zhou's 18°C)
  - Rolling OOS 2015–2024 (vs. Zhou's single forward year)
  - Zero risk premium
"""

